think Read KYRI, RADIANT_STYLE, REMEMBER, REDS, and the top session-log rows to seat the thread. Standfast clear -- every living REDS row (80, 83, 84, 85 and the prose notes) is closed or released; only #75 rests as custody-gated errata (a history rewrite, Keaton's hand). No agent-closable red booked, so the constructive queue is open.
think The last several logs named the crux-first next sibling with one voice: a DIFFERENTIAL TURNING DESCRIPTOR, the signed-curvature string over chain_code's ring, complementary to the shape number. Took it -- highest-Lindy of the named siblings (a convexity/corner family descends from it) and the honest complement of the freshly-landed shape number.
think Designed the composition before coding: shape_number reads chain_code's FIRST DIFFERENCE unsigned (0..7) and minimizes it to a canonical form; this rung reads the SAME first difference SIGNED, folding each digit to (-4, 4] so a right turn is positive and a left turn negative. One raw difference, two lenses -- magnitude for matching, sign for curvature. Proved that complementarity digit-for-digit in the witness against shape_number.first_difference (a contract check at the seam, exactly the happy-zone teaching this lap's rota doc names).
think First ambition was a CONVEXITY oracle via a per-step reflex threshold (a turn <= -2 marks a concave corner). MEASUREMENT BEAT MEMORY twice on metal: the size-5 triangle's 45-degree hypotenuse is a CLEAN diagonal run (constant code, turns 0), not a staircase, so it carried no -1 wobble -- my wobble assertion was a fixture over-claim (corrected: the triangle instead reads a +3 sharper-than-right-angle corner an axis rectangle never shows). Then the L's concave right angle spread into TWO -1 steps (codes 2,1,0 -> turns -1,-1), never a single -2 -- so the threshold missed the dent entirely.
think The honest reading: a raster concave right angle spreads into two -1 steps AND a shallow convex staircase also wobbles -1, so a per-step threshold cannot ROBUSTLY decide convexity. Retightened the rung to its unimpeachable core and deferred the oracle to a named sibling reading polygon's SIMPLIFIED vertices (where the staircase noise is already gone). Dropped reflex_count/is_convex/reflex_turn_threshold; kept turning_profile (the descriptor), total_turning (+8 Gauss-Bonnet, topological), total_absolute_turning (total heading variation), profile_has_negative (surfaces a dent, does not decide convexity).
think Two Zig subtleties caught by the compiler/output before any GREEN: a literal `{0,+2}` in the print string parsed as a format placeholder (too-few-arguments) -- reworded to "zero-or-plus-two"; and leftover is_convex references from the first draft in three fixtures -- all removed. No red booked: fixture over-claims and draft leftovers corrected before the first GREEN, the Standfast unbroken.
obs Compose not braid held: the rung owns only the signed fold and its reads; chain_code owns the code and its geometry, shape_number the unsigned canonical form. The digit-for-digit complementarity is the seam contract made checkable.
obs The +8 total is the beautiful topological anchor -- the SAME integer for a block, a triangle, an L, and a plus, indifferent to how dented the outline is -- while the SIGN and the heading variation are what the descriptor adds over the sign-blind shape number: they SEE a concavity the canonical form cannot represent at all.
obs Honesty over ambition paid: a robust convexity oracle would have shipped a claim I could not cleanly prove on rasters. The deferred sibling (turning over polygon's vertices) is now the crux-first next lap, well-named.
